                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "24426475",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198065549172",
                            "num_reviews": 47,
                            "playtime_forever": 30,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 30,
                            "last_played": 1469028243
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Before starting the review I have to state two important things:\n[list]\n[*] The game is made by one person\n[*] The game is still being development with many features planned\n[/list]\n\nDATH is a strange kind of game, and I mean it in a positive way. You start the game believing you're in a sort of unfinished game with no plot at all, and all you have to do is killing reptitive horde of enemies. At a certain point things start to change (I won't spoil it for you).\nDATH feels like a story of redemption, of second chances.\nI love the RPG features in a 2D game like that. It's an interesting mix that makes it strangely addictive.\nYou can purchase weapons, armors, potions, and all the necessary items to continue your journey.\nThe controls are simple, you have a basic and stronger attacks, spells and abilities; the levels, however, are quite hard, making it an extremely challenging title. It's  fast paced, with many enemies and traps lurking.\n\nAm I recommending the game? Yes.\nI like how it is coming along so far, and I know bigger updates are planned.\n\n",
